    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The app already does what you asked, so I didn't change anything. Both acceptance tests pass with `bin/e2e`: entering 0 is rejected with an error and no invoice is added, and entering 75 adds one invoice.\n\nA zero or negative amount is blocked in three places:\n\n- **Database:** `V4__create_invoice.sql` has a check, `invoice_amount_positive CHECK (amount > 0)`, so no new migration was needed.\n- **Server:** `InvoiceRequest.amount` requires a value of at least 0.01 (`@NotNull @DecimalMin(\"0.01\")`), and the controller checks it before saving. A bad amount gets a 400 error.\n- **Front end:** the invoice form in `project-invoices.ts` requires an amount of at least 0.01, which can't be negative and has at most two decimal places. If the amount is wrong, it shows the error message (`invoice-form-amount-error`) and doesn't send the request.\n\nOne small mismatch: your request said \"OfficeFloor server\", but the server is a standard Spring Boot app. \"OfficeFloor\" only appears in its package name (`net.officefloor.hq.app`).",
